hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"194","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani and Yusuf bin Musa told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, on the authority of Shurayh bin Hani said: I asked Aisha about wiping over the socks, and she said: Go to Ali and ask him, for he knows that more than me. Then he came to Ali and asked him about wiping over the socks, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order that. The resident should wipe over his socks day and night. And the traveler is three.”"
